window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Since her first appearance in the award-winning <b><i>Sunglasses After Dark</i></b>, Sonja Blue--the leather-clad female punk vampire/vampire slayer--has stalked the Undead who prey on an unwitting humanity at the cost of the lives of those she loves, her sanity, and what hope she might have to one day reach eternal rest. <b>Blue Murder </b>is the first collection of short stories and novelettes in over 20 years to feature the iconic vampire slayer and includes two never-before collected tales.<br> <br> In <i>Search and Destroy</i> Sonja hunts down the undead horror preying on a homeless encampment.<br> <i><br> Cold Turkey</i> deals with her attempt to rid herself of The Other--the demonic personality within herself she must constantly battle for control of her body.<br> <i><br> Tender Tigers</i> has her fighting to rescue a human girl from a family of ogres.<br> <i><br> Vampire King of the Goth Chicks</i> involves her investigation into a rumored blood cult operating out of an abandoned church. <i>Some Velvet Morning </i>tells the grim fairy tale of the mysterious Countess who must bathe in blood to maintain her youth and what happens when she crosses paths with Sonja Blue.<br> <br> In <i>Rancho Midnight</i>, Sonja travels to Sin City to make sure what happens in Vegas stays in Vegas, as she battles undying evil with her trademark balls-to-the-wall panache.<br> <br> And <i>Last Know Photo</i> sees her help a mother find her missing son.<br> No Sparkling Allowed.</p>"; 
